('91a79b03-63ba-4eb3-854f-94ef9f4bd149', 'Crunch Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '2741201', '02741201-Crunch-Floor-(male)_waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Crunch Floor. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Crunch Floor', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('91ac86ff-d523-4dff-83bc-9e03ab0265b6', 'Standing Front Elbow Touch To Overhead Cross', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Standing Front Elbow Touch To Overhead Cross, focusing on your abs. Your obliques work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '95461201', '95461201-Standing-Front-Elbow-Touch-to-Overhead-Cross-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Front Elbow Touch To Overhead Cross. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Front Elbow Touch To Overhead Cross', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('91b5199d-5efd-4a2e-9640-15dad35821ae', 'Superman Pulse', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Superman Pulse is a lower body movement exercise that targets your lower back. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '103451201', '103451201-Superman-Pulse-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 2. Set up in the starting position for Superman Pulse. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lower back. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Superman Pulse', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('91bac256-699f-4586-8135-279916e6e773', 'Sphinx Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Sphinx Push Up is an arm pushing exercise targeting your chest. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '71781201', '71781201-Sphinx-Push-Up-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Sphinx Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('91dfa962-c490-4892-9b48-e9b89a271d31', 'Shoulder Stretch Behind The Back (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '35131201', '35131201-Resistance-Band-Shoulder-Stretch-Behind-the-Back_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Shoulder Stretch Behind The Back. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band Shoulder Stretch Behind The Back. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 45, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Shoulder Stretch Behind The Back', 'stretch_chest, stretch_tricep, stretch_lat', FALSE, 'band', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('91e2495c-a416-4a12-b085-b516309ed2f5', 'Kneeling Shoulder Internal Rotation (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Kneeling Shoulder Internal Rotation is a rotation exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '67561201', '67561201-Cable-Kneeling-Shoulder-Internal-Rotation-(male)_B.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Kneeling Shoulder Internal Rotation. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Cable Kneeling Shoulder Internal Rotation. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Kneeling Shoulder Internal Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('91e2b8cb-5b12-41c1-8672-d4a8e8f17895', 'Scapular Slide Back To Wall (Wall)', 'Full Body', 'Wall', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Scapular Slide Back To Wall is a movement exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. You''ll also feel your rotator cuff working to support the movement. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '51851201', '51851201-Scapular-Slide-Back-to-Wall-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for Scapular Slide Back To Wall. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your upper back. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Scapular Slide Back To Wall', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('91ee3191-070f-404a-baf3-514124f2857e', 'Lying Elbow Press (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Lying Elbow Press is an arm pressing exercise targeting your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '3381201', '03381201-Dumbbell-Lying-Elbow-Press_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Elbow Press. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Elbow Press. 3. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Lying Elbow Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Elbow Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9203d873-9b29-4674-9e0e-dc8522d94703', 'Ball Sit Up (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '211201', '00211201-Ball-Sit-up-(on-stability-ball)_waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Ball Sit Up. 2. Set up in the starting position for Ball Sit Up. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Ball Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92059e0a-6f0f-480f-8ceb-0b9ce101f7a9', 'Lunge With Internal Rotation', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your quads, the Lunge With Internal Rotation helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '105281201', '105281201-Lunge-with-Internal-Rotation-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for Lunge With Internal Rotation. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Lunge With Internal Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92079772-fcf0-47d5-9087-d0c408744864', 'Wide Plank Side Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Wide Plank Side Tap is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '73421201', '73421201-Wide-Plank-Side-Tap-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Wide Plank Side Tap', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9212b6ef-ecc1-4e73-b431-891881b1d7e5', 'Side Bend (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Side Bend (stability Ball) is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '7001201', '07001201-Side-Bend-(on-stability-ball)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Side Bend. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92189384-b592-4d5c-b026-78a39b7ea84e', 'Swimmer Kicks', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Swimmer Kicks is a lower body kicking exercise that targets your full body. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '34341201', '34341201-Swimmer-Kicks-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Swimmer Kicks. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'swimming', 'Swimmer Kicks', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('923ae4e6-cbf5-4e27-9ead-0db43f6c4109', 'Standing Archer Butt Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic kicking movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '103091201', '103091201-Standing-Archer-Butt-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Archer Butt Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Standing Archer Butt Kick', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('923c2663-eb22-4fac-9913-9940431e2814', 'Incline Bicep Curl - Inner (Kettlebell)', 'Arms', 'Kettlebell, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '68221201', '68221201-Kettlebell-Incline-Inner-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Incline Inner Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 91, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Incline Inner Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('923ec624-54f3-4d35-89e2-500306b1ae9d', 'Side To Side Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your hamstrings, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. You''ll also feel your lower back working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '79201201', '79201201-Side-to-Side-Hamstring-Stretch-(female)_Stretching.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Side To Side Hamstring Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 28, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Side To Side Hamstring Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('92474e43-c98a-452b-a1f8-34f2c12816fb', 'Reverse Hyper (Stability Ball, Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band, Stability Ball', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your erector spinae with this movement exercise for a stronger posterior chain. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '67381201', '67381201-Resistance-Band-Reverse-Hyper-with-Stability-Ball-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Reverse Hyper. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band Reverse Hyper. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lower back. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 39, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Reverse Hyper', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9250025c-9b9a-4808-99d0-710212a11dd7', 'Lunge With Jump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '35821201', '35821201-Lunge-with-Jump_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Lunge With Jump', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('925433ce-c578-49bc-a291-72a0ca41b1d9', 'Iron Cross (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this movement movement focusing on your delts. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '36011201', '36011201-Dumbbell-Iron-Cross-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Iron Cross. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Iron Cross. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Iron Cross', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('92551fe2-de34-44c8-a4f5-2524fefa87fd', 'Standing Curl - Close Grip (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '26931201', '26931201-Barbell-Standing-Close-Grip-Curl-(female)_Upper-Ar.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Standing Close Grip Curl. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 4. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 5. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 6. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, 'Underhand', 'Narrow', 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Curl - Close Grip', 'Standing Curl - Close Grip', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
