('92757933-82e6-4318-94c6-472295937e57', 'Standing Hands Torsion (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Hands Torsion is an arm movement exercise targeting your full body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '70541201', '70541201-Dumbbell-Standing-Hands-Torsion-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Hands Torsion. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 64, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Hands Torsion', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('927c3747-4709-49dc-9068-2cc26ad6bc30', 'Glute Bridge From Bench', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Glute Bridge From Bench is a hip-dominant bridging exercise that targets your glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '80151201', '80151201-Glute-Bridge-from-Bench-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Glute Bridge From Bench', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('927e9261-226e-4726-b5ca-086114a4bc56', 'Rear Lunge From Step (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '23671201', '23671201-Dumbbell-Rear-Lunge-from-Step-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Rear Lunge From Step. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 4. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Rear Lunge From Step', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('928b015f-5b20-4ab0-adf6-55750fa42344', 'Single Arm Side Lying Bench Press (Flat Bench, Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbell One Arm Side Lying Bench Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '58161201', '58161201-Dumbell-One-Arm-Side-Lying-Bench-Press-(male)_Ches.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Dumbell Single Arm Side Lying Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('928f03ea-1f95-49e0-b0ae-4cadc18c5cbc', 'Side Step Front Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Front Plank is a lower body stabilization exercise that targets your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '39581201', '39581201-Side-Step-Front-Plank-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Side Step Front Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9290159a-e9f6-4a6d-8b5d-0fd00274de64', 'Palm Press Back', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this pressing movement. Your rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '63731201', '63731201-Palm-Press-Back-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Execute the pressing motion for Palm Press Back, extending through the target muscles. 2. Set up in the starting position for Palm Press Back. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your upper back. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Palm Press Back', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9296b718-e510-49f3-889e-ad9e91e6f9d7', 'Wide Chin Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this movement movement. You''ll also feel your biceps working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '81891201', '81891201-Wide-Chin-Up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 2. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Wide Chin Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92a86d8d-1259-4f66-99a6-27dc23021486', 'Standing Hip Thrust (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this thrusting movement that emphasizes the glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '98481201', '98481201-Lever-Standing-Hip-Thrust-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Standing Hip Thrust. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 4. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 5. Lower your hips back down with control. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Lever Standing Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('92b03ab7-3cbf-4b61-b353-f8e41f8c0528', 'Rear Delt Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your rear delts with the Bodyweight Rear Delt Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '94251201', '94251201-Bodyweight-Rear-Delt-Raise-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Raise your arms out to the sides and back, focusing on rear delts. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Rear Delt Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, face_pull, bent_over_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92b04257-759d-4fa1-955a-62826fc12d9b', '45 Degrees Single Leg Reverse Hyperextension (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Back', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The 45 Degrees Single Leg Reverse Hyperextension is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. Your hamstrings, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '69481201', '69481201-45-degrees-Single-Leg-Reverse-Hyperextension_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 2. Lower with control back to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', '45 Degrees Single Leg Reverse Hyperextension', 'leg_curl, squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92bbe0f6-60f9-4e83-a538-3e530e4dab8e', 'Kneeling Butterfly (Towel)', 'Chest', 'Towel', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this flying movement focusing on your chest. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '67061201', '67061201-Bodyweight-Kneeling-Butterfly-with-Towels-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Kneeling Butterfly With Towels', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92c1589d-055b-4d5d-a881-228d6900492d', 'Seated Lateral Neck Stretch (Chair)', 'Neck', 'Chair', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your neck, the Seated Lateral Neck Stretch On A Chair helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Secondary activation of your upper back provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '104701201', '104701201-Seated-Lateral-Neck-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(male)_Str.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Lateral Neck Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 27, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Seated Lateral Neck Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92cb9a15-b319-44ef-8485-08df22a3c39d', '90 To 90 (Stretch)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your hips, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '67101201', '67101201-90-to-90-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for 90 To 90 Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', 'Static / Mobility', 'Static', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated (Floor)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', '90 To 90', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92ddc81f-f9dc-402a-b42f-7fadca9b6768', 'Skullcrusher - Reverse Grip (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This movement movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '17211201', '17211201-Barbell-Reverse-Grip-Skullcrusher_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Reverse Grip Skullcrusher. 2. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Skullcrusher - Reverse Grip', 'Skullcrusher - Reverse Grip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('92e13751-36b5-4e9f-9dad-90a10b00ee7e', 'Behind The Back Clap', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this movement movement that develops pressing power. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '59961201', '59961201-Behind-the-Back-Clap-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Behind The Back Clap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Behind The Back Clap', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92e82d74-0c30-4721-abee-c2fd9f1154e2', 'Standing Around World (Wall Supported)', 'Shoulders', 'Wall', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this movement movement focusing on your delts. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '46121201', '46121201-Bodyweight-Standing-Around-World-Wall-Supported_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 44, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Around World Wall Supported', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92ef855c-c43b-4a7a-b7f9-a7423c5f6657', 'Burpee', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'The Burpee is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. The chest, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '27941201', '27941201-Burpee-(female)_Cardio-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 2. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 3. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Burpee', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('92f28f45-52db-4262-b722-8a88f961a835', 'Hurdle Hops (Hurdles)', 'Legs', 'Hurdles', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'The Hurdle Hops is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '69631201', '69631201-Hurdle-Hops-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Hurdle Hops. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hop', 'Hurdle Hops', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9306ed4e-ee12-41c3-8c78-12534c023f2a', 'Rotation Back Swing', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This rotation movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '83971201', '83971201-Rotation-Back-Swing-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Rotation Back Swing. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Rotation Back Swing', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('9327086b-d31d-44f1-8e2b-6b927c8d54a3', 'Deadlift From Deficit (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell, Step Platform', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '57021201', '57021201-Barbell-Deadlift-from-Deficit_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Deadlift From Deficit. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'deadlift', 'Deadlift From Deficit', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('93394dc0-14e5-4f95-8bdf-38f8513d6867', 'High Pull With Rope Attachment (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pulling movement focusing on your delts. Your traps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '66481201', '66481201-Cable-High-Pull-with-Rope-Attachment-(male)_Should.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable High Pull With Rope Attachment. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'upright_row', 'High Pull With Rope Attachment', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('9343cc6f-09b6-4537-8ca5-fc0365bd882c', 'Standing Double Elbow Knee Touch - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build total body strength and coordination with this multi-joint movement movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '93631201', '93631201-Standing-Alternating-Double-Elbow-Knee-Touch-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Standing Double Elbow Knee Touch - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9365e7fc-8f8e-429f-8496-d0e45dca035a', 'Front Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '4651201', '04651201-Front-Plank-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. This variation specifically emphasizes the abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('93852e4c-076a-4d83-9e1e-24762e738a50', 'Front Step Knee Drive - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '79501201', '79501201-Alternate-Front-Step-Knee-Drive-(female)_Plyometri.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Front Step Knee Drive - Alternating', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('938ab0da-e4bb-4e8c-abd1-06462baf2f89', 'Standing Switching Vertical Stacked Hand', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this movement movement that develops pressing power. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '97061201', '97061201-Standing-Switching-Vertical-Stacked-Hand-(male)_Ch.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Switching Vertical Stacked Hand. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Switching Vertical Stacked Hand', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('93928df9-638d-4a57-af37-c3622b939658', 'Standing Lateral Leg Circle (Chair)', 'Hips', 'Chair', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Standing Lateral Leg Circle With A Chair is a lower body movement exercise that targets your delts. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '84211201', '84211201-Standing-Lateral-Leg-Circle-with-a-Chair-(male)_Hi.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Lateral Leg Circle With A Chair', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('93969ee3-f6a4-4f42-8201-63bb61b5c662', 'Circle Draw - Underhand', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '76351201', '76351201-Underhand-Circle-Draw-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Use an underhand (supinated) grip with palms facing up/toward you. 2. Set up in the starting position for Underhand Circle Draw. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Underhand Circle Draw', 'Circle Draw - Underhand', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('939d4bb8-decf-4afd-94f5-c296bcebcd93', 'Kneeling Single Arm Cross Body Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Kneeling One Arm Cross Body Stretch provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '19881201', '19881201-Kneeling-One-Arm-Cross-Body-Stretch-(female)_Shoul.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling One Arm Cross Body Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 35, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Kneeling Single Arm Cross Body Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('93b74150-d2db-4616-8b0f-1e28d605a2da', 'Standing Shoulder Medial And Lateral Rotation', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This full-body rotation exercise challenges multiple muscle groups simultaneously. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '80611201', '80611201-Standing-Shoulder-Medial-and-Lateral-Rotation-(mal.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Shoulder Medial And Lateral Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Shoulder Medial And Lateral Rotation', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('93b9840f-2f30-4d96-a4a5-0e94970ec06c', 'Lying Reverse Abdominal Press', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Lying Reverse Abdominal Press, focusing on your abs. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '92911201', '92911201-Lying-Reverse-Abdominal-Press-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Reverse Abdominal Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Lying Reverse Abdominal Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Reverse Abdominal Press', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('93bbfc98-190b-4dcb-ab31-12440b30fad2', 'Standing Single Arm Chest Fly (Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Band Standing Single Arm Chest Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '86051201', '86051201-Band-Standing-Single-Arm-Chest-Fly-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Standing Single Arm Chest Fly. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Single Arm Chest Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('93c7ef5c-ebcd-432e-8355-3f7f6ff6dbc8', 'Dip On Floor (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dip On Floor With Chair, an effective dipping movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '38151201', '38151201-Dip-on-Floor-with-Chair-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dip On Floor With Chair. 3. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 4. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Dip On Floor With Chair', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('93dd055b-ae73-40ee-8e6d-c3e92bfe64c8', 'Jefferson Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this curling movement focusing on your biceps. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '73291201', '73291201-Dumbbell-Jefferson-Curl-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Jefferson Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Jefferson Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('93dd2a97-3574-4011-865f-813f05937b52', 'Crossover Heel Touch Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity squatting exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '105291201', '105291201-Crossover-Heel-Touch-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. An effective movement for your plyometrics routine.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Crossover Heel Touch Squat', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('93e77020-f34c-42d8-8a94-36effb0bda38', 'Seated Single Leg Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '89461201', '89461201-Seated-Single-Leg-Raise-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Single Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('93f5373b-06df-4ee1-8841-a134b4dd14f5', 'Full Swing (Kettlebell)', 'Full Body', 'Kettlebell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Full Swing is a compound swinging exercise that engages your entire body. Your glutes, core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '35711201', '35711201-Kettlebell-Full-Swing_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Full Swing. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Full Swing', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('93f55abd-2733-4464-b31e-b082d1f45cb7', 'Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '22531201', '22531201-Dumbbell-Fly-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('93f5980a-52a4-41eb-926c-6c4c18ec9b6a', 'Pull Apart (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Pull Apart is a pulling exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '97571201', '97571201-Resistance-Band-Pull-Apart-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Pull Apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band Pull Apart. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_apart', 'Pull Apart', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9404d7a1-e38c-4c80-9126-b1b82d559827', 'Kneeling Cat Cow Diagonal Reach Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your spine area and enhance overall flexibility. Your core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '82131201', '82131201-Kneeling-Cat-Cow-Diagonal-Reach-Stretch-(female)_S.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Cat Cow Diagonal Reach Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Kneeling Cat Cow Diagonal Reach Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('940b569b-e783-4fc8-b293-66f5ad64a6e8', 'Single Leg Dip On Floor', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This dipping movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '43641201', '43641201-Single-Leg-Dip-on-floor_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Single Leg Dip On Floor. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Single Leg Dip On Floor', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('941099b2-a0eb-4030-b1a7-0ff4dbc2c9fd', 'Uneven Pull Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Your biceps, upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '69611201', '69611201-Uneven-Pull-up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 2. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Uneven Pull Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9413e260-03c2-4425-a730-dcea47063679', 'Seated Side Circle Draw (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your delts. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '91181201', '91181201-Sitting-Side-Circle-Draw-on-a-Chair-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Ideal for delts strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Side Circle Draw On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('94200c40-d8bc-49ff-b320-2886da589576', 'Revolved Side Angle Pose Parivrtta Parsvakonasana', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '9571201', '09571201-Revolved-Side-Angle-Pose-Parivrtta-Parsvakonasana-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Revolved Side Angle Pose Parivrtta Parsvakonasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Revolved Side Angle Pose Parivrtta Parsvakonasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9421b342-66e9-4be3-ba05-83137be94ab5', 'Seated In Out Leg Raise On Floor - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '68511201', '68511201-Seated-Alternate-In-Out-Leg-Raise-on-Floor_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Seated Alternate In Out Leg Raise On Floor. 2. Sit on the floor with your legs positioned as required. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated In Out Leg Raise On Floor - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9424bbf9-6449-453a-a106-5340a6fa664c', 'Walk (Wave Machine)', 'Legs', 'Wave Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Walk Wave Machine is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '36251201', '36251201-Walk-Wave-Machine-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Walk Wave Machine. 2. Set up in the starting position for Walk Wave Machine. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Cardio', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Walk Wave', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('942a07c8-1757-4030-a375-edbe0bc182d1', 'Spinal Stretch (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '43141201', '43141201-Spinal-Stretch-(on-stability-ball)-(male)_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Spinal Stretch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Spinal Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 32, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'spinal_stretch', 'Spinal Stretch', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'stability_ball', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('942dc0e5-4c63-4103-a398-79ef138779a9', 'Ring Self Assisted Chin Up (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Back', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Your biceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '65001201', '65001201-Ring-Self-Assisted-Chin-Up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 2. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability. A solid choice for back day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Ring Self Assisted Chin Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('9431e0d5-65eb-484d-940d-3ef9bff1db5c', 'Roll Shoulder Back Rotation Lying On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Roll Shoulder Back Rotation Lying On Floor, focusing on your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '54191201', '54191201-Roll-Shoulder-Back-Rotation-Lying-on-Floor-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Shoulder Back Rotation Lying On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Roll Shoulder Back Rotation Lying On Floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Roll Shoulder Back Rotation Lying On Floor. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Roll Shoulder Back Rotation Lying On Floor', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9436a1b3-fbe6-4994-841f-4b943fd5bc50', 'Bicep Curl - Front Step', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Biceps Curl Front Step is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic curling movements. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '56231201', '56231201-Biceps-Curl-Front Step-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Biceps Curl Front Step', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('943e694a-b997-4859-91a0-9f524961be5e', 'Seated Shoulder Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Seated Shoulder Circle is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '87261201', '87261201-Seated-Shoulder-Circle-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Shoulder Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Seated Shoulder Circle', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('944bd410-6625-4c31-a414-1da4805cd644', 'Lying Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '3511201', '03511201-Dumbbell-Lying-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Triceps Extension. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Triceps Extension. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lying Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('94522455-63dc-468b-a654-99096db45bed', 'Glute Ham Developer Full Sit Up (Machine)', 'Legs', 'GHD Machine', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '106391201', '106391201-Glute-Ham-Developer-Full-Sit-up_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Glute Ham Developer Full Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Glute Ham Developer Full Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('94526692-4423-4d08-8775-c267316bb0b1', 'Standing Front Feet Tap To Knee Tuck - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Standing Alternating Front Feet Tap To Knee Tuck ( builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '91561201', '91561201-Standing-Alternating-Front-Feet-Tap-to-Knee-Tuck-(.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Front Feet Tap To Knee Tuck ( - Alternating', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('94583a50-72c7-442d-a848-a1967091f887', '45 Degree Single Leg Hyperextension (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Back', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The 45 Degree One Leg Hyperextension is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. Your hamstrings, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '11701201', '11701201-45-Degree-One-Leg-Hyperextension-(arms-in-front-of.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 2. Lower with control back to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', '45 Degree Single Leg Hyperextension', 'leg_curl, squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('946676ca-3160-4653-a0ad-8d208d144ce7', 'Downward Dog To Chest Press', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your chest, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your hamstrings, shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '85511201', '85511201-Downward-Dog-to-Chest-Press-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Move into the stretch position for Downward Dog To Chest Press. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Downward Dog To Chest Press', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9467d183-6bf7-478b-8844-3e269d47bd52', 'Shin Box Switch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Aim for full range of motion on every rep. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '106821201', '106821201-Shin-Box-Switch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Move into the stretch position for Shin Box Switch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Shin Box Switch', 'stretch_hip, dynamic_warmup, yoga_pose', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9469f7ca-9cd1-467e-bfed-fb8ed221b9a5', 'Mountain Climbers Shoulder Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Mountain Climbers Shoulder Tap builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your hip flexors, shoulders working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '55301201', '55301201-Mountain-Climbers-Shoulder-Tap-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. From plank position, drive one knee toward your chest. 2. Quickly switch legs, bringing the other knee forward. 3. Continue alternating at a quick pace while maintaining plank form. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Mountain Climbers Shoulder Tap', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('946d3af2-3f1c-4433-9293-bb749a792596', 'Standing Upper Back And Shoulder Stretch', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your upper back, the Standing Upper Back And Shoulder Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '73121201', '73121201-Standing-Upper-Back-and-Shoulder-Stretch-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Upper Back And Shoulder Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Standing Upper Back And Shoulder Stretch', 'stretch_chest, stretch_tricep, stretch_lat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9482d823-d3b9-4ea3-98af-8f64da708d48', 'Sumo Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '23221201', '23221201-Dumbbell-Sumo-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Sumo Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Sumo Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9483303e-a6a5-4162-9463-639a48aff330', 'Kneeling Twist Down Up Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Kneeling Twist Down Up Raise targets your obliques through a raising motion, building rotational core strength. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '85051201', '85051201-Dumbbell-Kneeling-Twist-Down-Up-Raise-(male)_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Kneeling Twist Down Up Raise. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Kneeling Twist Down Up Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Kneeling Twist Down Up Raise', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('94834211-6590-41d3-8713-f2524c29ccb2', 'Single Leg Bridge (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this bridging movement that emphasizes the glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '104011201', '104011201-Resistance-Band-Single-Leg-Bridge-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Single Leg Bridge. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Single Leg Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('948a70c9-9819-4cd6-862c-a253ac804c55', 'Rear Delt Row (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Rear Delt Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '37551201', '37551201-Dumbbell-Rear-Delt-Row-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Rear Delt Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'rear_delt', 'Rear Delt Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('948de31a-259f-48be-a288-070219e76eab', 'Deep Push Up And Renegade Row (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Back","Lats"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Deep Push Up And Renegade Row, an effective rowing movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '47361201', '47361201-Dumbbell-Deep-Push-up-and-Renegade-Row_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Deep Push Up And Renegade Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Deep Push Up And Renegade Row', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip, tricep_pushdown', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('949161d1-b2fe-405b-ba94-da547290f8fe', 'Pushdown (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Pushdown targets your triceps through a pushing motion. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '2011201', '02011201-Cable-Pushdown_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Pushdown. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('94a30459-d135-40ff-8fab-8233f57ea1a7', 'Standing Balance Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Standing Balance Quadriceps Stretch provides a deep stretch for your quads, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '63201201', '63201201-Standing-Balance-Quadriceps-Stretch-(female)_Stret.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Balance Quadriceps Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Standing Balance Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('94b75bfd-3d22-47a7-8cda-5369a26c24e5', 'Straight Arm Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this pulling movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '2381201', '02381201-Cable-Straight-Arm-Pulldown_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Straight Arm Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Straight Arm Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('94c9eceb-9ff1-4324-aa4e-c78f92f5ac46', 'Stepback Russian Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this twisting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '100621201', '100621201-Stepback-Russian-Twist-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Stepback Russian Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Stepback Russian Twist', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('94cb91b0-c568-479d-8dc3-cdaade053654', 'Twist Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '8221201', '08221201-Twist-Squat-(female)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. This exercise is excellent for quads development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Twist Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('94de53ac-f3b5-43c7-a758-419aac00c34f', 'Standing Scissors Jump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'The Standing Scissors Jump is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic jumping movements. The quads, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '43281201', '43281201-Standing-Scissors-Jump_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Scissors Jump. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 52, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Scissors Jump', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('94df9e09-05b1-4b39-b06d-9f9f6659d559', 'Seated To Intense Plantar Flexion', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this flexion stretch that helps restore range of motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '83891201', '83891201-Seated-to-Intense-Plantar-Flexion-(female)_Stretch.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated To Intense Plantar Flexion. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated To Intense Plantar Flexion', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('94e2844d-15a0-4ea5-a955-08723d2e78ad', 'Seated Single Leg Half Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your delts. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '107451201', '107451201-Seated-Single-Leg-Half-Circle-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Seated Single Leg Half Circle', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('94fe9407-09cf-4aed-9235-2ff395299c69', 'Broad Long Jump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Broad Long Jump builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your quads, calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '74561201', '74561201-Broad-Long-Jump-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Broad Long Jump. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Broad Long Jump', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('950372b1-6474-405c-a5b9-5c844a0c6189', 'Shoulders Stretch (Stick)', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '54011201', '54011201-Stick-Shoulders-Stretch-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Stick Shoulders Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Stick Shoulders Stretch', 'stretch_chest, stretch_tricep, stretch_lat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('95078b2b-9b78-4cb4-873e-13408dbe2d31', 'Leg Press (Plate Loaded) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this pressing exercise for quad development. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '22871201', '22871201-Lever-Alternate-Leg-Press-(plate-loaded)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Alternate Leg Press. 2. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 3. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Lever Leg Press - Alternating', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9507dff2-7c76-41d2-8132-33d8eb182888', 'Incline Single Arm Lat Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '83481201', '83481201-Cable-Incline-Single-Arm-Lat-Pulldown-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Incline Single Arm Lat Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Incline Single Arm Lat Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('950f7d0c-896d-4107-b884-547afafeaab0', 'Hanging Toes To Bar (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Hanging Toes To Bar is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors, grip provides additional muscle engagement. The hanging position challenges your grip while targeting the primary muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '101111201', '101111201-Hanging-Toes-to-Bar-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hanging Toes To Bar. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Hanging Toes To Bar', 'pull_up, lat_pulldown, grip_training', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9513da7d-9ec8-4074-9e48-fec9527221df', 'Incline Hip Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '90491201', '90491201-Incline-Hip-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Incline Hip Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Incline Hip Raise', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('95295fdc-9f49-4cb5-baa5-29cd1646b494', 'Across Chest Shoulder Stretch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stretching exercise that challenges your entire body. Your shoulders, core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '19801201', '19801201-Across-Chest-Shoulder-Stretch_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Across Chest Shoulder Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Across Chest Shoulder Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9533cdc9-b414-4a55-bc8b-82e2996359a5', 'Single Stiff Leg Deadlift (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '75671201', '75671201-Dumbbell-Single-Stiff-Leg-Deadlift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Single Stiff Leg Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('954058e2-b50f-472b-b0d3-944c875534f3', '45 Degrees Hyperextension (Resistance Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band 45 Degrees Hyperextension is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. Secondary activation of your hamstrings, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '38751201', '38751201-Resistance-Band-45-degrees-Hyperextension_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band 45 Degrees Hyperextension. 2. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', '45 Degrees Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('955493bc-aaca-47f2-b7f1-fbfeef6a2f95', 'Paused Sumo Deadlift (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Lower Back","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Paused Sumo Deadlift is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '55771201', '55771201-Barbell-Paused-Sumo-Deadlift_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Paused Sumo Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Pause for 1-3 seconds at the bottom or peak of the movement before continuing. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'deadlift', 'Paused Sumo Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9554bda5-dd15-4536-bc72-eb11f3ee22c5', 'Run And Half Knee Bend', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Enhance your stamina and burn calories with this effective cardio movement. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '32711201', '32711201-Run-and-Half-Knee-Bend-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Run And Half Knee Bend. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'running', 'Run And Half Knee Bend', 'cycling, rowing_cardio, jump_rope', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('955c9256-3c7d-43ba-a47a-0925e0e343a2', 'Overhead Sit Up With Legs On Bench (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Overhead Sit Up With Legs On Bench is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '68091201', '68091201-Dumbbell-Overhead-Sit-up-with-Legs-on-Bench-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Overhead Sit Up With Legs On Bench. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Overhead Sit Up With Legs On Bench. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Overhead Sit Up With Legs On Bench', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('95684d57-9655-42f3-9887-fbb6611af145', 'Dead Bug (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Dead Bug (stability Ball), focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '85081201', '85081201-Dead-Bug-with-Stability-Ball-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Dead Bug. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dead Bug. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dead_bug', 'Dead Bug', 'plank, bird_dog, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('956ee6ac-7f5f-4564-8b9c-937b72482f45', 'Sit Up Slam (Medicine Ball)', 'Core', 'Medicine Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '105581201', '105581201-Medicine-Ball-Sit-up-Slam-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Sit Up Slam. 2. Set up in the starting position for Medicine Ball Sit Up Slam. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Medicine Ball Sit Up Slam', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'medicine_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9575787e-dd4a-4910-9187-fa1e8171fb6d', 'Split Squat (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '88931201', '88931201-Kettlebell-Split-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Split Squat', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('958afd77-ac7b-441f-bd7b-72f8b883e0f9', 'Front Plank To Downward Dog', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stabilization exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '45001201', '45001201-Bodyweight-Front-Plank-to-Downward-Dog_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Front Plank To Downward Dog', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('95914e8e-1dfd-4097-9f93-292435a1b2fe', 'Press Under', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Press Under, a comprehensive pressing exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '106991201', '106991201-Press-Under-(female)_Weightlifting_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Execute the pressing motion for Press Under, extending through the target muscles. 2. Set up in the starting position for Press Under. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Press Under', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9592562d-74e0-4c4d-96c5-3ecf852200e8', 'Seated Chest Press (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '30611201', '30611201-Cable-Seated-Chest-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Chest Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Seated Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('95a9ea80-df4c-4144-bf33-dec997bf7071', 'Glute Abductors Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Hip Abductor/Adductor Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this pressing movement focused on hip extension. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '66161201', '66161201-Lever-Glute-Abductors-Press-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Glute Abductors Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Lever Glute Abductors Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Lever Glute Abductors Press', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('95ad03fc-61c9-44ff-8224-ea247a9d8fc6', 'Side Lying Diagonal Backward Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '67511201', '67511201-Side-Lying-Diagonal-Backward-Leg-Raise-(female)_Hi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Side Lying Diagonal Backward Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('95b284de-2042-47db-9191-d60dee2b837a', 'Long Distance Lunge (low Lunge)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '97011201', '97011201-Long-Distance-Lunge-(Low-Lunge)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Long Distance Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('95b40119-8f15-484c-863e-d52aa650acc4', 'Lying Calf Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted stretching exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '49291201', '49291201-Lying-Calf-Stretch-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Calf Stretch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Calf Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_stretch', 'Lying Calf Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('95b6f1b9-7656-40ae-8ca6-97e0e55ad2ee', 'Angled Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this pressing movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '83751201', '83751201-Lever-Angled-Leg-Press-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Angled Leg Press. 2. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 3. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Lever Angled Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('95b909bc-b872-4a8a-a902-e2ebcef55468', 'Seated Squat Calf Raise (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '57851201', '57851201-Lever-Seated-Squat-Calf-Raise-on-Leg-Press-Machine.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Squat Calf Raise On Leg Press Machine. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 4. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Lever Seated Squat Calf Raise On Leg Press', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('95bd13d1-1c96-430d-bab3-5ad60e9d2eaf', 'Lying Side Bend', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your obliques, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. You''ll also feel your lats, lower back working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '94011201', '94011201-Lying-Side-Bend-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Side Bend. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Lying Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('95c62ac2-cb4c-4b4a-8a63-cb5b4053707b', 'Single Leg Squat (Stability Ball)', 'Legs', 'Stability Ball', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '16951201', '16951201-Stability-Ball-Single-Leg-Squat_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Stability Ball Single Leg Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Stability Ball Single Leg Squat', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('95dbc6e6-d5cb-4e63-9402-68eea5f9bf02', 'Decline Push Up - Weighted Vest (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Chest', 'Gymnastic Rings, Weighted Vest', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '78751201', '78751201-Ring-Weighted-Vest-Decline-Push-up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', 'Push Up', 'Push', NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 61, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Ring Weighted Vest Decline Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('95f66a8f-19f9-426a-a850-5c7700b8f687', 'Standing Top Clap Back Clap', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your back, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '68991201', '68991201-Standing-Top-Clap-Back-Clap-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Top Clap Back Clap. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Top Clap Back Clap', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('95fd1971-596d-417c-8938-b4dbafdb8fb5', '45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focused (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Legs', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this extension movement focused on hip extension. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '93141201', '93141201-45-Degree-Hip-Extension-Glute-Focused-(VERSION-2)-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Extend through the target joint(s) for 45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focused. 2. Set up in the starting position for 45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focused. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', '45 Degree Hip Extension Glute Focused', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('96035b74-ee44-4b3f-916e-41dee43234bd', 'High Knee Walk', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Calves"}'::text[], 'The High Knee Walk is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '107591201', '107591201-High-Knee-Walk-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for High Knee Walk. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'High Knee Walk', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9610dd8c-f9a5-463a-a570-30500ce9fa70', 'Shoulder Press (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Cable Shoulder Press, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '2191201', '02191201-Cable-Shoulder-Press_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Shoulder Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('9613ae35-79f4-4e63-8d35-05ff7f592990', 'Prisoner High Knee', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '71861201', '71861201-Prisoner-High-Knee-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Prisoner High Knee. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'Prisoner High Knee', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('963848c3-0e17-4326-9380-12667a8d360c', 'Cheat Curl', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '56961201', '56961201-Cheat-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Cheat Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('96417d7b-b989-4299-8f55-29a25ebfdb49', 'Lying Prone Ys', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Lying Prone Ys is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '58001201', '58001201-Bodyweight-Lying-Prone-Ys_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Lie face down with your body in a straight line. 2. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Lying Prone Ys. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Prone Ys', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('964fcfe8-cea2-4606-a73c-efcac7ea06df', 'Incline Front Raise (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Incline Front Raise is a raising exercise that targets your front delts for shoulder development. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '96481201', '96481201-Barbell-Incline-Front-Raise_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Incline Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Incline Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('96520736-0e73-49ce-a83f-4ab29c6fe16d', 'Upright Row (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Cable Upright Row, an effective shoulder rowing exercise. Secondary activation of your traps provides additional muscle engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '2461201', '02461201-Cable-Upright-Row_Shoulders-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Upright Row. 2. Pull the weight straight up along your body, leading with your elbows. 3. Raise until elbows reach shoulder height, then lower with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'upright_row', 'Upright Row', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, shrug', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('96528e82-9fb5-4854-a068-b5ebfbd8b2a9', 'Standing Inner Curl (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing Inner Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '2291201', '02291201-Cable-Standing-Inner-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Inner Curl. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Inner Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('96591785-cff4-4a25-a4d0-1308fe4ab090', 'Deadlift (Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '46181201', '46181201-Band-Deadlift_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'deadlift', 'Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('965e936f-88e3-42d7-b194-34f8ea62db98', 'Seated Back Rotation (Chair) - Alternating', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this rotation movement targeting your core. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '87891201', '87891201-Seated-Alternate-Back-Rotation-on-a-Chair-(male)_B.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Alternate Back Rotation On A Chair. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Seated Back Rotation On A Chair - Alternating', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('965f77b6-25a4-4f72-b864-66655f56be5e', 'Subscapularis Muscle Relax (Stick)', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Stick Subscapularis Muscle Relax provides a deep stretch for your upper back, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '68111201', '68111201-Stick-Subscapularis-Muscle-Relax-(male)_Stretching.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Stick Subscapularis Muscle Relax. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Stick Subscapularis Muscle Relax', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9674d345-647b-4d10-a858-008033db5ded', 'Standing Front Triple Arm Cross And Top Triple Arm', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Front Triple Arm Cross And Top Triple Arm is a compound movement exercise that engages your entire body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '94291201', '94291201-Standing-Front-Triple-Arm-Cross-and-Top-Triple-Arm.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Front Triple Arm Cross And Top Triple Arm. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Front Triple Arm Cross And Top Triple Arm', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('96973851-8484-4c08-a757-e6b5e93251b6', 'Incline Front Raise (EZ Bar)', 'Shoulders', 'EZ Bar', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your front delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '39891201', '39891201-EZ-bar-Incline-Front-Raise_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Grip the EZ bar on the angled portions for a comfortable wrist position. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'EZ Bar Incline Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('96a612cc-4dab-438c-a7e3-9d1ff74151cc', 'Single Arm Low Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '97491201', '97491201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Low-Fly-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Single Arm Low Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('96aee11a-461d-44d1-9f32-b64e12fac65e', 'Assisted Chin Tuck', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Assisted Chin Tuck targets your neck muscles through a controlled movement motion. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Include this exercise in your routine for balanced strength development.', '31521201', '31521201-Assisted-Chin-Tuck-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Assisted Chin Tuck. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your neck. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Assisted Chin Tuck', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('96db7c13-f25c-40e5-a323-28aa16edbd0c', 'Elbow Closed Arms Pulse', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Elbow Closed Arms Pulse is a movement exercise that targets your chest muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '76381201', '76381201-Elbow-Closed-Arms-Pulse-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 2. Set up in the starting position for Elbow Closed Arms Pulse. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pulse', 'Elbow Closed Arms Pulse', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('96df4a03-c3d5-4262-b572-38e014510a91', 'Sit Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '15931201', '15931201-Sit-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. This variation specifically emphasizes the quads.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Sit Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('96e93817-ba89-4461-8df1-6e638af97776', 'Seated Internal And External Shoulder Rotation', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this rotation movement focusing on your rotator cuff. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '87241201', '87241201-Seated-Internal-and-External-Shoulder-Rotation-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Internal And External Shoulder Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Seated Internal And External Shoulder Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('96f3ad61-e51f-4ac4-ad94-5bca25a52717', 'Standing Rear Kick (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this kicking movement that emphasizes the glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '10371201', '10371201-Lever-Standing-Rear-Kick_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Standing Rear Kick. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lever Standing Rear Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('96f7e8d4-c33a-40bc-a373-97a67a99baa3', 'Shoulder Bridge', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your shoulders, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '28631201', '28631201-Shoulder-Bridge-(female)_Pilates_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Shoulder Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('96fa8c86-0487-42ad-a8a8-31587f262bf9', 'Rotational Jacks', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '6831201', '06831201-Rotational-Jacks-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Rotational Jacks. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 42, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Rotational Jacks', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97082040-52c0-484a-9406-2f7ee1331136', 'Dip (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This dipping exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '70271201', '70271201-Dips-between-Chairs-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. An effective movement for your chest routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Dip Between Chairs', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('970b3c10-e014-4f04-8512-e4b5ef23a9b7', 'Stepback With Hands Raise', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads"}'::text[], 'This dynamic raising movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '44341201', '44341201-Stepback-with-Hands-Raise_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Stepback With Hands Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Stepback With Hands Raise', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('971ed370-72ac-4285-acd0-f72d7ca50cb5', 'Overhead Triceps Extension (Kettlebell)', 'Arms', 'Kettlebell', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '58601201', '58601201-Kettlebell-Overhead-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Overhead Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('9720a6e4-5746-4de5-b60b-befc818cc880', 'Half Moon Pose Ardha Chandrasana', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '9521201', '09521201-Half-Moon-Pose-Ardha-Chandrasana-(female)_Stretchi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Half Moon Pose Ardha Chandrasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Half Moon Pose Ardha Chandrasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('972230b3-1bf5-4c10-be11-da0a868f2635', 'Elevated Heel Front Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells, Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '96901201', '96901201-Dumbbell-Elevated-Heel-Front-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Elevated Heel Front Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'front_squat', 'Elevated Heel Front Squat', 'squat, leg_press, leg_extension, goblet_squat', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('972410e1-1a6f-4cd2-88fb-46a07c01f252', 'Lying Knee Flexion - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Alternate Knee Flexion is a lower body flexion exercise that targets your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '79401201', '79401201-Lying-Alternate-Knee-Flexion-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Alternate Knee Flexion. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Knee Flexion - Alternating', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9732d5ad-314e-4760-9da6-d91bee460020', 'Twist Knee Up Punch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity twisting exercise that challenges your entire body. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '78261201', '78261201-Twist-Knee-Up-Punch-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist Knee Up Punch. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist Knee Up Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('973b4cbf-c3b0-482a-8701-ab21f182acf9', 'Incline Chest Press (Plate Loaded Machine)', 'Chest', 'Chest Press Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Lever Incline Chest Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '70901201', '70901201-Lever-Incline-Chest-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Incline Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 81, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Lever Incline Chest Press', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('973d1e19-2524-48d1-8abc-c0413f105f94', 'Bear Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this squatting movement that works your abs. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '97121201', '97121201-Bear-Squat-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Works well for abs activation.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Bear Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9745bf54-a2fb-43c5-87bc-040053db98ca', 'Back Shrug (Smith Machine)', 'Back', 'Smith Machine', '{Trapezius}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Smith Back Shrug is a shrugging exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '107091201', '107091201-Smith-Back-Shrug-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Back Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Smith Back Shrug', 'Back Shrug', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9746580d-1c43-48c5-a7cd-28fef2d99ef0', 'Side Squat Jack', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Side Squat Jack is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic squatting movements. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '78571201', '78571201-Side-Squat-Jack-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Squat Jack', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9749fab0-e037-4fb2-99b6-94b2727cc346', '90 To 90 (Alternating) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '96561201', '96561201-90-to-90-(beginner)-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for 90 To 90. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', 'Static / Mobility', 'Static', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', '90 To 90', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97560c77-e4d1-42e3-a818-2f3026967db2', 'Kneeling Stay Forward Wheel Rollout (Ab Wheel)', 'Core', 'Ab Wheel', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Kneeling Stay Forward Wheel Rollout, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your lats, shoulders working to support the movement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '77711201', '77711201-Kneeling-Stay-Forward-Wheel-Rollout-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Stay Forward Wheel Rollout. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'ab_rollout', 'Kneeling Stay Forward Wheel Rollout', 'plank, crunch, dead_bug', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97569a37-9c7b-42b5-a60e-7e1fe7c6728a', 'Straight Back Seated Row (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cable Straight Back Seated Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. You''ll also feel your biceps, lats working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '30691201', '30691201-Cable-Straight-Back-Seated-Row-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Straight Back Seated Row. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Straight Back Seated Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('97667586-94d4-49a4-ab6a-63eaefc00265', 'High Bar Incline Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The High Bar Incline Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '93121201', '93121201-High-Bar-Incline-Push-up-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Include this in your chest training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'High Bar Incline Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97711700-b2a1-4bca-b4df-2daa9b77d2b7', 'Incline Reverse Raise With Chest Supported Skier (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '66101201', '66101201-Dumbbell-Incline-Reverse-Raise-with-Chest-Supported-(skier)-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Reverse Raise With Chest Supported. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Incline Reverse Raise With Chest Supported. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Incline Reverse Raise With Chest Supported', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9773e12c-7223-466b-bc37-bc51bf4cb8bf', 'Rowing (Rowing Machine)', 'Back', 'Row Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Rowing (with Rowing Machine) is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. You''ll also feel your biceps, rear delts working to support the movement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '11611201', '11611201-Rowing-(with-rowing-machine)_Cardio-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Rowing. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'rowing_machine', 'Rowing', 'cycling, running, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('97742fb0-06a6-4505-87fc-83ed684bbac0', 'Lying Crossed Stacked Arms Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Lying Crossed Stacked Arms Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '95581201', '95581201-Lying-Crossed-Stacked-Arms-Stretch-(female)_Stretc.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Crossed Stacked Arms Stretch. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Crossed Stacked Arms Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Lying Crossed Stacked Arms Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97774049-5f68-45b1-a02a-ef8da9b6e13c', 'Weighted Twisting Crunch (On Bench)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this crunching exercise that strengthens your obliques. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '11881201', '11881201-Weighted-Twisting-Crunch-(on-bench)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. Include this in your core training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Weighted Twisting Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97826d5f-ea07-4e2e-a60f-f33dff64ae88', 'Reverse Fly (TRX)', 'Shoulders', 'TRX', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise works your rear delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Secondary activation of your upper back provides additional muscle engagement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '10901201', '10901201-Suspender-Reverse-Fly-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Reverse Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Suspender Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('97870918-95de-48f5-9dd3-f25238698572', 'Seated Single Chest Stretch (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '91761201', '91761201-Sitting-Single-Chest-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(female)_S.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Single Chest Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 6. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Seated Single Chest Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('978991d4-9710-4d83-a51b-55b4b76bced3', 'Downward Dog Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your abs, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The hamstrings, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '64161201', '64161201-Downward-Dog-Leg-Raise-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 2. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 3. Move into the stretch position for Downward Dog Leg Raise. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Downward Dog Leg Raise', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97942e66-bb2a-4a22-a15a-02a25746134c', 'Bench Press - Close Grip (Smith Machine)', 'Chest', 'Smith Machine, Flat Bench', '{Triceps}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Smith Close Grip Bench Press targets your triceps through a pressing motion. Secondary activation of your chest provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '74001201', '74001201-Smith-Close-Grip-Bench-Press-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Close Grip Bench Press. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'close_grip_bench', 'Smith Bench Press - Close Grip', 'Bench Press - Close Grip', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('979b6aff-2a4f-4dca-9120-5ada9379be4f', 'Figure 8 March', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Figure 8 March is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '91571201', '91571201-Figure-8-March-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Figure 8 March. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Figure 8 March', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('979f07b6-372c-4c3f-99d3-9ff0cf2a2f0b', 'Knee Raise Side Reach - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Alternate Knee Raise Side Reach builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '89081201', '89081201-Alternate-Knee-Raise-Side-Reach-(male)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Knee Raise Side Reach - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97af26e3-2e0d-4109-b265-e30262991c17', 'Shoulder Abduction', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Shoulder Abduction is a movement exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '88391201', '88391201-Shoulder---Abduction-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Shoulder Abduction. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Shoulder Abduction', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97b1da14-e266-4ef3-8764-d8aa1bf92ef4', 'Bent Over Row (Resistance Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Back","Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. Your biceps, lats work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '91271201', '91271201-Resistance-Band-Bent-Over-Row-(VERSION-2)-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Bent Over Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bent_over_row', 'Bent Over Row', 'cable_row, dumbbell_row, t_bar_row, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('97ba0ee0-50db-457a-a172-96155e5f8b22', 'Seated Shoulder Internal Rotation (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Seated Shoulder Internal Rotation is a rotation exercise that targets your chest muscles. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '2161201', '02161201-Cable-Seated-Shoulder-Internal-Rotation_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Shoulder Internal Rotation. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Cable Seated Shoulder Internal Rotation. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Seated Shoulder Internal Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('97bc23f5-8575-4251-b013-1574a1905eb2', 'Standing Triple Arm Cross', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders, core working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '97111201', '97111201-Standing-Triple-Arm-Cross-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Triple Arm Cross. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Triple Arm Cross', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97bfd5f3-adb4-4c32-993b-2f7a103c4106', 'Lying Shoulder External Rotation', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Lying Shoulder External Rotation is a rotation exercise that targets your rotator cuff for shoulder development. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '67541201', '67541201-Bodyweight-Lying-Shoulder-External-Rotation-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Bodyweight Lying Shoulder External Rotation. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Bodyweight Lying Shoulder External Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Lying Shoulder External Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97c1d2b5-0cf1-46a7-9e02-b626c055b5b1', 'Cobra Pose (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '93301201', '93301201-Cobra-Pose-on-Stability-Ball-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Cobra Pose. 2. Move into the stretch position for Cobra Pose. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Cobra Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'stability_ball', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97c9691e-e408-4c5d-b73d-8a6fccd9a9a9', 'Seated Forward Bend Stretch (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your hamstrings, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '84331201', '84331201-Seated-Forward-Bend-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(male)_Stre.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Forward Bend Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 27, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Seated Forward Bend Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97d43e20-fd01-494f-85e4-6ba97a3f8895', 'Standing Switching Palm Squeezes', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Switching Palm Squeezes is an arm movement exercise targeting your full body. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '65821201', '65821201-Standing-Switching-Palm-Squeezes-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Switching Palm Squeezes. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Switching Palm Squeezes', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97d5ae37-400b-4c9f-a0d0-242a90830b92', 'Seated Corkscrew (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Corkscrew On A Chair is a lower body movement exercise that targets your obliques. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '92811201', '92811201-Sitting-Corkscrew-on-a-Chair-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. Beneficial for overall legs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Corkscrew On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97dd40e7-cc72-47a8-94e6-575e2a2977a0', 'Kneeling Cat Cow Look Back', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your spine area and enhance overall flexibility. The core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '82121201', '82121201-Kneeling-Cat-Cow-Look-Back-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Cat Cow Look Back. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Kneeling Cat Cow Look Back', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97dd62ba-65de-4a84-9db0-55eb95d860d0', 'Standing Balance Glute Kickback (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Standing Balance Glute Kickback (V is a hip-dominant kicking exercise that targets your glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '80911201', '80911201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Balance-Glute-Kickback-(V.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Balance Glute Kickback (V. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 4. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 39, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Standing Balance Glute Kickback', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('97e15e29-105a-42cf-8613-cb865b633d76', 'Seated Neck Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your neck, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '61701201', '61701201-Sitting-Neck-Stretch-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Neck Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Seated Neck Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97e60226-e848-4b2a-87c6-a5640743ec48', 'Over Bench Single Arm Neutral Wrist Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Over Bench One Arm Neutral Wrist Curl strengthens your forearms and grip through a curling motion. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '26291201', '26291201-Dumbbell-Over-Bench-One-Arm-Neutral-Wrist-Curl-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Over Bench Single Arm Neutral Wrist Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('97ea81ea-9aab-476a-b89d-c417ba785b3d', 'Squat To Side Leg', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity squatting exercise that challenges your entire body. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '45021201', '45021201-Bodyweight-Squat-to-Side-Leg_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. A solid choice for plyometrics day.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat To Side Leg', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97eb4ce4-242a-4d5c-9c0d-4eebc20c3f1c', 'Frog Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Frog Crunch, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '80571201', '80571201-Frog-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. Beneficial for overall core development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Frog Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('97ebb6ae-09d9-48ed-bb79-2d616ac7ed7e', 'Front Lateral Raise (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Band Front Lateral Raise is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '39751201', '39751201-Band-front-lateral-raise-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Front Lateral Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Front Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('981b10b0-225c-4854-a2fa-3c9493465ede', 'Incline Bicep Curl (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '68461201', '68461201-Band-Incline-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Incline Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Incline Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9837d5f6-3f33-463a-bd8f-8ed38fadf3c0', 'Ring Pullover (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Chest', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pulling movement targeting your chest. You''ll also feel your lats, triceps working to support the movement. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '87501201', '87501201-Ring-Pullover-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 2. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 38, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Ring Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('9844e0db-ca1b-4e33-b672-efe4a23ea8d1', 'Crab Knee To Elbow', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '73311201', '73311201-Crab-Knee-to-Elbow-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Crab Knee To Elbow. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Crab Knee To Elbow', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('984cc155-b721-49e5-9066-f3b4f109df0f', 'Stepback Diagonal Punch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Stepback Diagonal Punch is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '98981201', '98981201-Stepback-Diagonal-Punch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Stepback Diagonal Punch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Stepback Diagonal Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9854e887-60af-4dec-a640-193bc11e115e', 'Reverse Fly (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Reverse Fly is a flying exercise that targets your rear delts for shoulder development. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '68291201', '68291201-Kettlebell-Reverse-Fly_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Reverse Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('98559454-cfb4-462e-b278-e6c7eda37c2a', 'Seated 8 Leg Crunch (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '71391201', '71391201-Seated-8-Leg-Crunch-with-Chair_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Seated 8 Leg Crunch With Chair', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9861ac98-6608-41e8-8171-24041ac446c5', 'Low Cross Front Leg Lift', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '97821201', '97821201-Low-Cross-Front-Leg-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Low Cross Front Leg Lift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Low Cross Front Leg Lift', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('988ac888-f6bf-4a01-91a7-29f24e646288', 'Standing Front Raise Drive (Plate)', 'Shoulders', 'Weight Plate', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your front delts, the Weighted Plate Standing Front Raise Drive helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '88241201', '88241201-Weighted-Plate-Standing-Front-Raise-Drive-(male)_S.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Weighted Plate Standing Front Raise Drive', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9894b81b-0099-42a9-83e4-b59772dcebc0', 'Seated In Out Leg Raise Over Bench', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Seated In Out Leg Raise Over Bench, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '78071201', '78071201-Seated-In-Out-Leg-Raise-over-Bench_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated In Out Leg Raise Over Bench', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('98a077fb-7a56-4229-b814-018bedb7bdb7', 'Preacher Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '24971201', '24971201-Barbell-Preacher-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, 'Underhand (Supinated)', 'Standard', 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('98a43084-04d7-4e61-8e28-62ac0e856bec', 'Deadlift (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Deadlift 360 Degrees is a hip hinge exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Your glutes, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '24841201', '24841201-Dumbbell-Deadlift-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Deadlift 360 Degrees. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'deadlift', 'Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('98a5d1d6-4845-40a5-9254-0bbd0c1c9ed8', 'Seated Palms Up Wrist Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this curling exercise. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '26331201', '26331201-Dumbbell-Seated-Palms-Up-Wrist-Curl-(female)_Forea.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Palms Up Wrist Curl. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Seated Palms Up Wrist Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('98bcce70-f2e3-4c92-8671-602ecd550e51', 'Farmers Walk', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Core","Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Farmers Walk is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. You''ll also feel your traps working to support the movement. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '57761201', '57761201-Farmers-walk-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Farmers Walk. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Farmers Walk', 'deadlift, shrug, suitcase_carry', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('98e97db6-d6cc-4528-ab90-f5f05f96dad4', 'Standing Chest Press (Band) - Alternating', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '70321201', '70321201-Band-Standing-Alternate-Chest-Press-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Standing Alternate Chest Press. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Standing Chest Press - Alternating', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('98ee9f25-39eb-4acd-b482-a62fa05add3d', 'Shoulder External Rotation In Support (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your rotator cuff with the Dumbbell Shoulder External Rotation In Support, an effective shoulder rotation exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '91941201', '91941201-Dumbbell-Shoulder-External-Rotation-in-Support-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Shoulder External Rotation In Support. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Dumbbell Shoulder External Rotation In Support. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Shoulder External Rotation In Support', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('98fed3bc-ff8f-4375-b015-36f788214645', 'Side Two Front Toe Touching', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '32511201', '32511201-Side-Two-Front-Toe-Touching-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Two Front Toe Touching. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'toe_touch', 'Side Two Front Toe Touching', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('98ff14c5-2c12-4b8c-a571-ab3075fee708', 'Standing Iron Eagle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '90261201', '90261201-Standing-Iron-Eagle-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Iron Eagle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Iron Eagle', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9912a247-964c-4c34-a369-00353dfd9b16', 'Seated Face Pull Rope (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Cable Seated Face Pull (with Rope), an effective shoulder pulling exercise. Your upper back, rotator cuff work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '56581201', '56581201-Cable-Seated-Face-Pull-(with-rope)-(male)_Shoulder.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Face Pull. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the rope toward your face, separating your hands as you pull. 4. Squeeze your rear delts and upper back at peak contraction. 5. Return with control, maintaining cable tension. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'face_pull', 'Seated Face Pull', 'rear_delt_fly, bent_over_row, lateral_raise', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('9921e161-72ca-4e4e-ba09-201ad13a416f', 'Body Slide', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '51381201', '51381201-Body-Slide-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Body Slide. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Body Slide', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('993183d4-5e3a-4717-ae54-85908ede38d8', 'Lying Crunch (Plate)', 'Core', 'Weight Plate', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '107101201', '107101201-Weighted-Plate-Lying-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Weighted Plate Lying Crunch. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Weighted Plate Lying Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9941c12a-8deb-445c-901b-2c1e85f31699', 'Lying Double Glute Lift Heel Tap', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this movement movement focused on hip extension. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '94501201', '94501201-Lying-Double-Glute-Lift-Heel-Tap-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Double Glute Lift Heel Tap. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Double Glute Lift Heel Tap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Lying Double Glute Lift Heel Tap', 'crunch, bicycle_crunch, russian_twist', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('995bad94-0398-46c0-9fd9-84fdee5dfa0f', 'Preacher Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '3701201', '03701201-Dumbbell-Peacher-Hammer-Curl_Forearms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Peacher Hammer Curl. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hammer_curl', 'Peacher Hammer Curl', 'bicep_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('995e7ca5-6824-41f3-88a2-bafcbc6c5c62', 'Seated Neck Rotation (Chair)', 'Neck', 'Chair', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Seated Neck Rotation On A Chair targets your neck muscles through a controlled rotation motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this exercise in your routine for balanced strength development.', '92641201', '92641201-Sitting-Neck-Rotation-on-a-Chair-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Neck Rotation On A Chair. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Seated Neck Rotation On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('997daa8c-7c7e-4862-b860-ac890d7ddcfa', 'Seated Knee Up Extended Rotation Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Seated Knee Up Extended Rotation Stretch provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '19341201', '19341201-Seated-Knee-Up-Extended-Rotation-Stretch-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Knee Up Extended Rotation Stretch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Knee Up Extended Rotation Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('997f1ef7-4331-4354-a0d2-a9ae4d240a06', 'Seated Behind Back Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Behind Back Raise is a raising exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '51331201', '51331201-Seated-Behind-Back-Raise-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Seated Behind Back Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Seated Behind Back Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9981a610-d865-405c-a02d-b701142c9d65', 'Standing Arms Out Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Standing Arms Out Twist targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '94701201', '94701201-Standing-Arms-Out-Twist-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Arms Out Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Standing Arms Out Twist', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('99852e7c-b093-431d-aa60-6c0f737b4c82', 'Leg Curl (Stability Ball)', 'Legs', 'Stability Ball', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. The calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '5691201', '05691201-Leg-Curl-(on-stability-ball)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Leg Curl. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9996995a-ca81-4b2e-908e-d11105d3164c', 'Lying Woodchop (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Dumbbell Lying Woodchop. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '47471201', '47471201-Dumbbell-Lying-Woodchop_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Woodchop. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Woodchop. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 62, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Lying Woodchop', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('99978bbd-929f-49af-9ed0-2fe4c88e3cfa', 'Lying Around The World', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this movement movement focusing on your delts. The chest assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '65921201', '65921201-Lying-Around-the-World-(SIDE-POV)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Around The World. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'around_world', 'Lying Around The World', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9998d8f7-43fe-442b-8399-ab3564efa838', 'Squat Air Bike (Air Bike)', 'Legs', 'Air Bike', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity squatting exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '77051201', '77051201-Squat-Air-Bike-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. A solid choice for plyometrics day. Variation: Squat Air Bike.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 70, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat Air Bike', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('99aa784e-35b5-44ee-9a75-9036ecf4c3fe', 'Double Punch Knee Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity raising exercise that challenges your entire body. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '67791201', '67791201-Double-Punch-Knee-Raise-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Double Punch Knee Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Double Punch Knee Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('99afb5e5-d361-4104-93eb-64f716a0f922', 'Lying Floor Single Leg Negative Dragon Flag', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '93221201', '93221201-Lying-Floor-Single-Leg-Negative-Dragon-Flag_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Lying Floor Single Leg Negative Dragon Flag. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Floor Single Leg Negative Dragon Flag. 3. Focus on a slow, controlled lowering phase (3-5 seconds). 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Lying Floor Single Leg Negative Dragon Flag', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('99affae0-1460-4cfe-9e0b-423a67328a2e', 'Star Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Star Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '56141201', '56141201-Star-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Star Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('99b6a7ba-5d1e-41ce-a2f4-3350131f4043', 'Wide Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '66021201', '66021201-Dumbbell-Wide-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Wide Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Wide Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('99b74ae4-a47b-41a4-b1e2-3e441e732843', 'Standing Lift (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing Lift is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. The standing position engages your core for stability. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '2301201', '02301201-Cable-Standing-Lift_waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Lift. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Standing Lift', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('99b81765-2b94-4239-a2be-b6d6af7a3215', 'Side Plank Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '74731201', '74731201-Dumbbell-Side-Plank-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Side Plank Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', TRUE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('99d72b5d-8c10-4731-891a-d1ee21c5d5bf', 'Forward Lunge (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '74661201', '74661201-Kettlebell-Forward-Lunge-(VERSION-2)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Forward Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Forward Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('99f93004-eb84-4973-9017-a7010bc25934', 'Seated Leg Curl (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Curl Machine', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Leg Curl targets your hamstrings through a controlled curling motion. Your calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '5991201', '05991201-Lever-Seated-Leg-Curl_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Leg Curl. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Lever Seated Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9a06d655-77cb-42ae-9231-81a33e3b5061', 'Glute Ham Sit Up', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Glute Ham Sit Up is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '65541201', '65541201-Glute-Ham-Sit-up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Glute Ham Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Glute Ham Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a1821a5-8a87-4e5e-9b9b-efe2e038ed3c', 'Goblet Lateral Step Up (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell, Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this stepping movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '80121201', '80121201-Kettlebell-Goblet-Lateral-Step-Up-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Goblet Lateral Step Up. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 4. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 5. Step back down with control and repeat. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Goblet Lateral Step Up', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('9a1f65c9-58e3-4a9e-b90b-69616a5bb348', 'Burpee (Kettlebell)', 'Full Body', 'Kettlebell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Kettlebell Burpee builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your chest, quads working to support the movement. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '38641201', '38641201-Kettlebell-Burpee_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Burpee. 2. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 3. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 4. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 58, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Burpee', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('9a248a59-c0ae-4a7f-8ef9-364d3677c46b', 'Standing Arms And Hip Circle', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Standing Arms And Hip Circle builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '93641201', '93641201-Standing-Arms-and-Hip-Circle-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Arms And Hip Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_circle', 'Standing Arms And Hip Circle', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a3077ad-7334-4e47-a543-c64560a0cc04', 'Squat Abductors', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this squatting movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '96351201', '96351201-Squat-Abductors-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Ideal for glute med/abductors strength and endurance.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Squat Abductors', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a310672-d0c9-46b1-9657-63cc1645ded9', 'Seated Swimming Knee Raise (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Seated Swimming Knee Raise On A Chair, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '82041201', '82041201-Sitting-Swimming-Knee-Raise-on-a-Chair-(male)_Wais.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Seated Swimming Knee Raise On A Chair. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Swimming Knee Raise On A Chair', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a3ae403-b1ea-4aba-a9dd-ed4943efb618', 'Standing Top Clap And Prayer Push', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Top Clap And Prayer Push is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '94761201', '94761201-Standing-Top-Clap-And-Prayer-Push-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Top Clap And Prayer Push. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Top Clap And Prayer Push', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a42fae0-dd7d-49e1-a1a3-4e3184cb0cd9', 'Single Arm Floor Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Barbell One Arm Floor Press is an arm pressing exercise targeting your chest. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '651201', '00651201-Barbell-One-Arm-Floor-Press_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Place a loaded barbell on the floor in front of you. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Barbell One Arm Floor Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Single Arm Floor Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9a5275ff-4c84-454e-891e-8a40e3749399', 'Old School Reverse Extension', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '52631201', '52631201-Old-School-Reverse-Extensions-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Extend through the target joint(s) for Old School Reverse Extensions. 2. Set up in the starting position for Old School Reverse Extensions. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Old School Reverse Extension', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a5ab70c-9303-409c-9a3d-95102369414c', 'Side Lunge Stretch (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Side Lunge Stretch provides a deep stretch for your quads, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '93091201', '93091201-Resistance-Band-Side-Lunge-Stretch-(VERSION-2)-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Side Lunge Stretch. 2. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 65, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Side Lunge Stretch', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9a6077c3-37fb-4418-8918-5d589468a5b8', 'Side To Side Punches', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Side To Side Punches is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '84091201', '84091201-Side-to-Side-Punches-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side To Side Punches. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Side To Side Punches', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a6fee5b-25e0-46d5-a969-1d49893dae30', 'Squat To Straddle', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Squat To Straddle provides a deep stretch for your quads, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '79091201', '79091201-Squat-to-Straddle-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Squat To Straddle', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a735f9b-b225-4ea5-9dfe-a1d505e69592', 'Fly (Kettlebell)', 'Chest', 'Kettlebell', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Kettlebell Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '66211201', '66211201-Kettlebell-Fly-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('9a7620f5-d9a1-4554-a812-7e63142fe9a5', 'Front Elbow Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '4631201', '04631201-Front-Elbow-Plank-(male)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. This variation specifically emphasizes the abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Elbow Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a782daa-0823-446c-a37d-d5ad24caf062', 'Seated Side Neck Stretch (Chair)', 'Neck', 'Chair', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your neck, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '91651201', '91651201-Sitting-Side-Neck-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(female)_Stre.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Side Neck Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 6. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Seated Side Neck Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a873dfd-2b11-4fa7-9b0a-072d2fc773d1', 'Dynamic Knee Drop', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dynamic Knee Drop is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '85711201', '85711201-Dynamic-Knee-Drop-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Dynamic Knee Drop. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Dynamic Knee Drop', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9a940513-4738-4ea0-b6ec-7a3dc7f6508c', 'Suspended Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '8061201', '08061201-Suspended-Push-Up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Suspended Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9ab1880d-d8d2-47c9-bf0e-428a9192fb5d', 'Single Arm Shoulder Press (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Band Single Arm Shoulder Press is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Your triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '81071201', '81071201-Band-Single-Arm-Shoulder-Press-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Single Arm Shoulder Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Single Arm Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9ab526fd-b36d-4247-acc4-a1ef66d7f294', 'Plank Jack', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Plank Jack is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '39301201', '39301201-Plank-Jack_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Jack', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('9ac525b7-e6fc-4601-b171-6539cbaa440d', 'Bench Front Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '30251201', '30251201-Barbell-Bench-Front-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'front_squat', 'Bench Front Squat', 'squat, leg_press, leg_extension, goblet_squat', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9ae88830-f440-4db8-9b41-7b66e6db3d3e', 'High Knee Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this squatting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '46361201', '46361201-High-Knee-Squat-(VERSION-3)-(male)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Beneficial for overall plyometrics development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'High Knee Squat', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9aec2b26-5c2d-40ef-93d2-69cdb1224fd2', 'Standing Bicep Curl - Arms United', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '105251201', '105251201-Standing-United-Biceps-Curl-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing United Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9aff9c93-a25e-40d6-aba2-2a3f6965bc5f', 'Sprinter Skip', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'The Sprinter Skip is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '75291201', '75291201-Sprinter-Skip-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Sprinter Skip. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'sprint', 'Sprinter Skip', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9b1a0ece-fe4d-4ccc-ac19-998cd2bbebe7', 'Box Jump Through The Arms (Plyo Box)', 'Legs', 'Plyo Box', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Calves"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity jumping exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your quads, calves working to support the movement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '107381201', '107381201-Box-Jump-Through-the-Arms-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Box Jump Through The Arms. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'box_jump', 'Box Jump Through The Arms', 'squat, burpee, broad_jump', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9b342eb4-2c02-4396-95ea-54aa22e7f61e', 'Hanging Pike (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Forearms"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors, grip working to support the movement. Hanging adds a grip and core stability component to the exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '4731201', '04731201-Hanging-Pike_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hanging Pike. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Hanging Pike', 'pull_up, lat_pulldown, grip_training', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9b37433a-7847-4b00-a217-e430f62267b4', 'High Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The High Lunge provides a deep stretch for your quads, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '73801201', '73801201-High-Lunge-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for High Lunge. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'High Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9b38e168-4319-49db-b125-e84451612945', 'Incline Bench Press (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Cable Incline Bench Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '1691201', '01691201-Cable-Incline-Bench-Press_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Incline Bench Press. 2. Set the bench to an incline angle (30-45 degrees). 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 98, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Incline Bench Press', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('9b4d82bd-e46f-4056-bcfb-f056a2b512ef', 'Good Morning', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Glutes"}'::text[], 'This movement movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '55551201', '55551201-Bodyweight-Good-Morning_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Good Morning. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Good Morning', 'romanian_deadlift, back_extension, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9b515ff4-571a-43b1-9259-3b5c6962d189', 'Squat Press Up', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this pressing movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '76751201', '76751201-Squat-Press-Up-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Execute the pressing motion for Squat Press Up, extending through the target muscles. 2. Set up in the starting position for Squat Press Up. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your quads. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Squat Press Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9b74bca9-6ce7-48a6-838e-09db6468ef18', 'Squat 2 Sec Hold (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '43621201', '43621201-Barbell-Squat-2-sec-Hold_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Squat 2 Sec Hold. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat 2 Sec Hold', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9b7ad2aa-70d7-420a-b2d0-d4ffbeaf606c', 'Standing Hip Extension (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this extension movement focused on hip extension. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '8801201', '08801201-Cable-standing-hip-extension-(version-2)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Hip Extension. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Cable Standing Hip Extension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Standing Hip Extension', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('9b7f4abb-ba5a-4d24-b17d-a53f21072345', 'Surrender Side Bend', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Surrender Side Bend is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '55861201', '55861201-Surrender-Side-Bend-(Male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Surrender Side Bend. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Surrender Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9b9e6abd-b8cc-4290-ab72-988a41424e87', 'Side To Side Quick Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '81341201', '81341201-Side-to-Side-Quick-Step-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side To Side Quick Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side To Side Quick Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9bac0871-40d1-4107-9dff-7a64219f70db', 'Cross Body Single Arm Chest Press (Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Band Cross Body One Arm Chest Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '70361201', '70361201-Band-Cross-Body-One-Arm-Chest-Press-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Cross Body One Arm Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Cross Body Single Arm Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9bc5a4e9-e85e-43f1-ae8c-3abc4cd1f4d5', 'High Row - Reverse Grip (Machine)', 'Back', 'Row Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '43781201', '43781201-Lever-Reverse-Grip-High-Row-(plate-loaded)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Reverse Grip High Row. 2. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'cable_row', 'Lever High Row - Reverse Grip', 'Lever High Row - Reverse Grip', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9bd18d37-bab7-43ca-8d07-97f242d5e3c8', 'Kneeling Straight Leg Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your delts. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '64141201', '64141201-Kneeling-Straight-Leg-Circle-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Straight Leg Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Kneeling Straight Leg Circle', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9bd7d48d-fe98-4e92-b49b-9e669502b117', 'Walk In And Out Arm Swing', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic swinging movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '89831201', '89831201-Walk-In-and-Out-Arm-Swing-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Walk In And Out Arm Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9bf1111b-248f-4e2b-b08e-77ec9cff7c5d', 'Seated Quick Step (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Seated Quick Step On A Chair builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '104761201', '104761201-Seated-Quick-Step-on-a-Chair-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Ideal for full body strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Quick Step On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9bf62556-feac-4f74-9ce1-ae74ab4b43d1', 'Seated Crossover - Underhand (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Seated Underhand Crossover On A Chair, an effective movement movement for upper body strength. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '91101201', '91101201-Sitting-Underhand-Crossover-on-a-Chair-(female)_Ch.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Use an underhand (supinated) grip with palms facing up/toward you. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Seated Underhand Crossover On A Chair', 'Sitting Crossover On A Chair - Underhand', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c01beca-8c2a-4579-9a4d-0c7a8ccd8372', 'Butterfly Pose Forward', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your adductors, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Secondary activation of your hips provides additional muscle engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '61331201', '61331201-Butterfly-Pose-Forward-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 2. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 3. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 70, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Butterfly Pose Forward', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c08d30d-06a3-4ac9-8fa8-2a4a1c30f6d5', 'Goblet Squat (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '65441201', '65441201-Cable-Goblet-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Goblet Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'goblet_squat', 'Goblet Squat', 'squat, front_squat, lunge', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('9c0c2058-77a7-40ee-8a18-86b1bcedb18d', 'Wide Kneeling Hip Thrust', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'The Wide Kneeling Hip Thrust is a hip-dominant thrusting exercise that targets your glutes. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '73461201', '73461201-Wide-Kneeling-Hip-Thrust-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Wide Kneeling Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c0d52f6-63df-4478-888a-29870c6ca479', 'Single Leg Lift (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your hip flexors. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '76671201', '76671201-Single-Leg-Lift-on-a-Chair-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 30, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Single Leg Lift On A Chair', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c0ea63b-6ce6-4076-8fa2-0bbc32b8e9a5', 'Self Assisted Inverse Leg Curl', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. Your calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '35071201', '35071201-Self-Assisted-Inverse-Leg-Curl-(VERSION-2)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 2. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 3. Extend legs back out with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Self Assisted Inverse Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c0fd20b-a46f-491f-88f5-baeddfe1a909', 'Iron Cross (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '3321201', '03321201-Dumbbell-Iron-Cross_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Iron Cross. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Iron Cross. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Iron Cross', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9c15c200-a6e0-43ca-a1f3-c4144eb4aeae', 'Seated Lotus Pose Twisting Front Back Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Seated Lotus Pose Twisting Front Back Tap. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '54871201', '54871201-Sitting-Lotus-Pose-Twisting-Front-Back-Tap-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Lotus Pose Twisting Front Back Tap. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Seated Lotus Pose Twisting Front Back Tap', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c1f84aa-3355-42a5-aa65-21fdf0db0cd6', 'Puppy Pose', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Puppy Pose is a flexibility exercise that targets your shoulders, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Your upper back, chest work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '58971201', '58971201-Puppy-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Puppy Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Puppy Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c20f514-1816-4c2a-89dd-18cf592bf0e3', 'Plank Pass Through (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '54971201', '54971201-Dumbbell-Plank-Pass-Through_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Plank Pass Through. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pass_through', 'Plank Pass Through', 'crunch, leg_raise, russian_twist, dead_bug', FALSE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9c25f66b-7d2d-4b2b-aab2-1261efefe113', 'Lying Bent Knee Side Roll', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Lying Bent Knee Side Roll, focusing on your abs. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '72431201', '72431201-Lying-Bent-Knee-Side-Roll-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Bent Knee Side Roll. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Bent Knee Side Roll', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c290fa0-f0e7-45d6-8491-67036df2a3dd', 'Full Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '57181201', '57181201-Barbell-Full-Squat-(Side-POV)-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Full Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 89, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Full Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9c31c4df-6c2f-4527-ab4c-1825cd68ec3f', 'Seated Single Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '97311201', '97311201-Lever-Seated-Single-Leg-Press-(VERSION-2)-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Single Leg Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 4. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Lever Seated Single Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9c3baa55-3aee-4385-ba01-756b86a58623', 'Bent Over Row With Chest Support - Neutral Grip (Machine)', 'Back', 'Row Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '65141201', '65141201-Lever-Bent-Over-Neutral-Grip-Row-(with-chest-support)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Bent Over Neutral Grip Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 68, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'chest_exercise', 'Lever Bent Over Row - Neutral Grip', 'Lever Bent Over Row - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9c44478e-7728-4117-9d88-b2ec145999db', 'Push Up On Forearms', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this pushing exercise. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '70851201', '70851201-Push-up-on-Forearms-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. Perfect for targeting your forearms.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Push Up On Forearms', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c505554-87b4-4617-b8b9-7dd48ec9d881', 'Judo Flip (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Cable Judo Flip is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '30531201', '30531201-Cable-Judo-Flip-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Judo Flip. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Judo Flip. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Judo Flip', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('9c577624-31ec-4521-ab76-c45190c81632', 'Elbow To Knee Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Elbow To Knee Sit Up is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '70281201', '70281201-Elbow-to-Knee-Sit-up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Elbow To Knee Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Elbow To Knee Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c584671-db08-4743-9c24-2e28763dd7b2', 'Change Lateral Raise Curtsey Lunge (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads","Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This lunging exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '72661201', '72661201-Dumbbell-Change-Lateral-Raise-Curtsey-Lunge-(male).mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Change Lateral Raise Curtsey Lunge. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Change Lateral Raise Curtsey Lunge', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
