('9c729907-925c-4d1d-9448-a1eae923e3fe', 'Decline Bench Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Decline Bench', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '24521201', '24521201-Dumbbell-Decline-Bench-Press-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Decline Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Decline Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'decline_press', 'Decline Bench Press', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9c90bbd7-04cb-40ce-8041-227939d78326', 'Elbow Touch And Lift', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '68981201', '68981201-Elbow-Touch-and-Lift-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Elbow Touch And Lift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Elbow Touch And Lift', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9c945218-1554-4a77-8189-dae934fe7252', 'Single Arm Twisting Seated Row (Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps, lats assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '38431201', '38431201-Band-One-Arm-Twisting-Seated-Row-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band One Arm Twisting Seated Row. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Single Arm Twisting Seated Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9c9f9d3f-3087-4be2-8b95-a43724dada87', 'Step Up (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells, Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stepping movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '22211201', '22211201-Dumbbell-Step-Up-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Step Up. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 4. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 5. Step back down with control and repeat. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Step Up', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9ca3ca17-ce14-475f-8496-b4e432ffc877', 'Seated I And T Raise (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your delts. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '104861201', '104861201-Seated-I-and-T-Raise-on-Chair-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Seated I And T Raise On Chair. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Seated I And T Raise On Chair', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9cab1bcb-8e0b-4f3e-99d1-392404e26e76', 'Seated Lumbar Spine Extension', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your spine, the Seated Lumbar Spine Extension helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Your lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '93261201', '93261201-Sitting-Lumbar-Spine-Extension-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Extend through the target joint(s) for Seated Lumbar Spine Extension. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Lumbar Spine Extension. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Seated Lumbar Spine Extension', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9cc7af30-da92-4dd9-a7ba-6c62af282b63', 'Kneeling Leg Out Side Walk', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Leg Out Side Walk provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '82141201', '82141201-Kneeling-Leg-Out-Side-Walk-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Leg Out Side Walk. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Kneeling Leg Out Side Walk', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9cdb01e7-be71-441f-86ec-407ab11e7583', 'Standing Side Crunch Elbow To Knee', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Standing Side Crunch Elbow To Knee is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '54991201', '54991201-Standing-Side-Crunch-Elbow-to-Knee-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Standing Side Crunch Elbow To Knee', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9cee085d-3ebd-455d-b25a-e5493718b2dd', 'Rotator Cuff Stretch', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Rotator Cuff Stretch is a stretching exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '19841201', '19841201-Rotator-Cuff-Stretch-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Rotator Cuff Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Rotator Cuff Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9cfe129a-8bed-46e5-8abe-7a20e94a6e9d', 'Front Seated Row (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cable Front Seated Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. The biceps, lats assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '73681201', '73681201-Cable-Front-Seated-Row-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Front Seated Row. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Front Seated Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('9d0c635d-dace-4a39-8f95-843e1203367d', 'Front Kick Twist', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity twisting exercise that challenges your entire body. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '87871201', '87871201-Front-Kick-Twist-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Front Kick Twist. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Front Kick Twist', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9d0d6db4-88e9-48ee-8eda-53a8a93d74ad', 'Arm Thruster (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build total body strength and coordination with this multi-joint thrusting movement. The quads, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '96931201', '96931201-Dumbbell-Alternating-Arm-Thruster_Weightlifting_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Alternating Arm Thruster. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'thruster', 'Arm Thruster - Alternating', 'front_squat, shoulder_press, clean', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9d14957d-4ab4-40dc-a9f7-23bec5837ba9', 'Seated Skater (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '84251201', '84251201-Seated-Skater-on-a-Chair-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 37, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'skater', 'Seated Skater On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9d18d4c9-228f-4a02-95fe-d9006948f4d1', 'Weighted Table Top Bridge (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This bridging exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '79381201', '79381201-Weighted-Dumbbell-Table-Top-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Weighted Dumbbell Table Top Bridge. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Weighted Table Top Bridge', 'Weighted Table Top Bridge', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9d1cb792-2f45-4e86-bd36-5c865132d85e', 'Roll Glutes Seated On Floor', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this movement movement that emphasizes the glutes. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '54281201', '54281201-Roll-Glutes-Sitting-on-Floor-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Glutes Seated On Floor. 2. Sit on the floor with your legs positioned as required. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Roll Glutes Seated On Floor', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9d1e61a3-6ea1-42ee-9769-ea757d4b05f6', 'Straigh Arm Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this pulling movement. Your biceps, upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '10671201', '10671201-Cable-straight-arm-pulldown-II-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Straigh Arm Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Straigh Arm Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('9d1fe53b-14d0-46e5-afc8-1d2ba7a986fe', 'Duck Walk (Resistance Band)', 'Full Body', 'Resistance Band', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Duck Walk is a lower body stepping exercise that targets your full body. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '24171201', '24171201-Resistance-Band-Duck-Walk-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Duck Walk. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band Duck Walk. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Duck Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9d24a98b-510a-439a-9dc8-9e05effc4f45', 'Kneeling Leg Half Circle On Bench (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Resistance Band Kneeling Leg Half Circle On Bench, an effective shoulder movement exercise. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '67411201', '67411201-Resistance-Band-Kneeling-Leg-Half-Circle-on-bench-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Kneeling Leg Half Circle On Bench. 2. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Kneeling Leg Half Circle On Bench', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9d279b94-6147-43e9-99cd-c9b2a6056158', 'Split Squat Front Foot Elevated (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Split Squat Front Foot Elevanted is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '77701201', '77701201-Barbell-Split-Squat-Front-Foot-Elevanted_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Split Squat Front Foot Elevanted. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Split Squat Front Foot Elevanted', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9d2f31d7-830d-45c9-8930-45aaa4bef86f', 'Split Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '23681201', '23681201-Split-Squats_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Ideal for quads strength and endurance.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Split Squat', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9d32cf5e-13db-49a0-8e9e-80702f1c8e15', 'Incline Rear Delt Row (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Incline Rear Delt Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '58531201', '58531201-Barbell-Incline-Rear-Delt-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Incline Rear Delt Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'rear_delt', 'Incline Rear Delt Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9d39b8a0-3a48-4d40-a1ea-587c3c9bf4ac', 'Seated Overhead Lats Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Seated Overhead Lats Stretch provides a deep stretch for your lats, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '104531201', '104531201-Sitting-Overhead-Lats-Stretch_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Overhead Lats Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Overhead Lats Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9d3be109-dc60-4082-b43a-5135f06b3688', 'Overhead Crunch (Stability Ball, Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell, Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '83281201', '83281201-Kettlebell-Overhead-Crunch-(on-stability-ball)_Wai.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Overhead Crunch. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Overhead Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('9d43dfeb-1074-4104-a31d-9bc0ad5b53ea', 'Side Step Crossover Arms', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stepping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '76971201', '76971201-Side-Step-Crossover-Arms-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Crossover Arms. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Side Step Crossover Arms', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9d58a3cc-7654-4d7b-8b15-ae70ba7a7c5f', 'Seated Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Seated Quadriceps Stretch provides a deep stretch for your quads, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '75621201', '75621201-Seated-Quadriceps-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Quadriceps Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9d725382-ac4c-48eb-aaa6-7da14daec281', 'Upright Row (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this rowing movement focusing on your delts. Your traps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '1211201', '01211201-Barbell-Upright-Row_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Upright Row. 2. Pull the weight straight up along your body, leading with your elbows. 3. Raise until elbows reach shoulder height, then lower with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'upright_row', 'Upright Row', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, shrug', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9d73c09f-5d0d-4359-82f5-272ea7d5b34f', 'Zottman Preacher Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '22941201', '22941201-Dumbbell-Zottman-Preacher-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Zottman Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Zottman Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9dad5f00-d8f4-488b-bd55-286bf86aa2cc', 'Svend Press', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Bodyweight Svend Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '59931201', '59931201-Bodyweight-Svend-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.60311+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Great for building strength in your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squeeze_press', 'Svend Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9db0364e-09d5-4fc7-8cba-260d62bfb954', 'Hands Up Knee Drive', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '93731201', '93731201-Hands-Up-Knee-Drive-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Hands Up Knee Drive. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Hands Up Knee Drive', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9dbee17f-bb64-4b40-957d-854e1551ed2d', 'Twist Down Up (Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Band Twist (down Up) targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '9311201', '09311201-Band-twist-(down-up)-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Band Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('9dc1f51e-8715-481a-9fcf-06fa53224038', 'Side To Front Bend Stretch (Stick)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Stick Side To Front Bend Stretch, focusing on your abs. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '54061201', '54061201-Stick-Side-to-Front-Bend-Stretch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Stick Side To Front Bend Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Stick Side To Front Bend Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9ded2dec-ec60-4bf5-a854-18fa6b38423e', 'Ankle Touch - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '56381201', '56381201-Alternating-Ankle-Touch-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 2. Set up in the starting position for Alternating Ankle Touch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, 'Compound', 'Bilateral (Alternating)', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Ankle Touch - Alternating', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9dee5005-279d-4544-8aa3-064f9a55db4a', 'Knees And Toes Point In Squat Slide (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '87721201', '87721201-Knees-and-Toes-Point-In-Squat-Slide-Wall-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Knees And Toes Point In Squat Slide Wall', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9df683ef-874b-4438-9fd2-d647eb582bf9', 'Front Plank To Side Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Front Plank To Side Plank, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '69251201', '69251201-Front-Plank-to-Side-Plank-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Front Plank To Side Plank', 'plank, russian_twist, woodchop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e00990e-c95b-4610-abc0-e0d1b308ac48', 'Double Twist Knee Up', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this twisting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '64751201', '64751201-Double-Twist-Knee-Up-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Double Twist Knee Up. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Double Twist Knee Up', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e0183a8-f19e-416a-a662-6cae7882a469', 'Seated Reverse Fly Parallel Grip (Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Fly Machine', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this flying movement focusing on your rear delts. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '6011201', '06011201-Lever-Seated-Reverse-Fly-(parallel-grip)_shoulder.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Reverse Fly. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Lever Seated Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9e0616c3-2332-4aa2-8728-376a6f297174', 'Standing Archer 45 Degrees Arm Row - Alternating', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '85861201', '85861201-Standing-Archer-Alternate-45-Degrees-Arm-Row-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Archer 45 Degrees Arm Row - Alternating', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e0b9b05-6c6b-42f1-9c25-a73f74d67dc7', 'Row (Kettlebell) - Alternating', 'Back', 'Kettlebell', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Alternating Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '5221201', '05221201-Kettlebell-Alternating-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Alternating Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Row - Alternating', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('9e162e3a-dfe0-4b9e-a77c-2b036dc2bb52', 'Arm Raise Back Leg Swing', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Arm Raise Back Leg Swing is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic raising movements. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '84741201', '84741201-Arm-Raise-Back-Leg-Swing-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Arm Raise Back Leg Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e17954a-e789-4d6f-9a82-bb5ab18865ab', 'Preacher Curl (Machine)', 'Arms', 'Preacher Curl Machine', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '5921201', '05921201-Lever-Preacher-Curl_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Lever Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9e212e25-b7af-4aa3-b2a2-5c50882560bf', 'Spider Crawl Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this pushing movement focusing on your chest. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '7781201', '07781201-Spider-Crawl-Push-up_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Perfect for targeting your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Spider Crawl Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e21467b-0ded-47c0-9143-69ba4d9e1cbd', 'Standing Scapular Rotation', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Scapular Rotation (front Pov) is a rotation exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '72321201', '72321201-Standing-Scapular-Rotation-(back-POV)-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Scapular Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Scapular Rotation', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e22742d-42d0-4a71-abdd-25dbd7a185dd', 'Reverse Preacher Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '811201', '00811201-Barbell-Reverse-Preacher-Curl_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Reverse Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Reverse Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9e270799-c4b9-4fb0-8b9b-bb5e6dc74801', 'Shoulder Level Test', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your shoulders with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Secondary activation of your upper back provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '67921201', '67921201-Shoulder-Level-Test-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Shoulder Level Test. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Shoulder Level Test', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e2c6818-1889-4f45-9611-5cd0330af2d2', 'Seated Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Dumbbell Seated Shoulder Press, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '22371201', '22371201-Dumbbell-Seated-Shoulder-Press-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Shoulder Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Seated Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9e30a9cd-b087-4e88-b377-582817bc7e0a', 'Torso Scissors (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Torso Scissors (stability Ball) is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '93311201', '93311201-Torso-Scissors-on-Stability-Ball-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Torso Scissors. 2. Set up in the starting position for Torso Scissors. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Torso Scissors', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e36ad23-c154-4254-92e1-058b02ff3d81', 'Sled 45 Degrees Leg Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Press Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Sled 45 Degrees Leg Press is a pressing exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '22241201', '22241201-Sled-45-degrees-Leg-Press-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 2. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Sled 45 Degrees Leg Press', 'squat, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9e409b7d-29a3-4c50-aff0-991f699375c2', 'Decline Sit Up - Twist Weighted Vest (Decline Bench)', 'Core', 'Decline Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This twisting movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '69371201', '69371201-Weighted-Decline-Twist-Sit-up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Weighted Decline Twist Sit Up. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Sit Up', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Weighted Decline Twist Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e4569be-2d79-4050-9ed0-c084b2ca277a', 'Pike Push Up With Parallettes', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '77501201', '77501201-Pike-Push-up-with-parallettes-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. Include this in your shoulders training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Pike Push Up With Parallettes', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e486906-b000-4722-97b7-704d428f1b47', 'Sumo Deadlift (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Lower Back","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '47591201', '47591201-Dumbbell-Sumo-Deadlift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Sumo Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'deadlift', 'Sumo Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('9e4d3f73-1d81-46d4-a5ef-376c94fd4815', 'Squat (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '87151201', '87151201-Lever-Squat-(plate-loaded)-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Lever Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9e4d41a5-0988-437e-a31a-1e5f611ab26f', 'Arms Straight Russian Twist (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this twisting exercise that strengthens your obliques. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '6861201', '06861201-Russian-Twist-(on-stability-ball-arms-straight)_Wa.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Arms Straight Russian Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Arms Straight Russian Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Arms Straight Russian Twist', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e5409c0-30ee-44fa-afe1-5374d0044de7', 'Squat And Tip Toes', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '61751201', '61751201-Squat-and-Tip-Toes-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Great for building strength in your quads.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Squat And Tip Toes', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e6b3e9d-3faf-4832-aa79-06eba2841ed4', 'Lying Elbow Touch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This movement exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '90341201', '90341201-Lying-Elbow-Touch-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Elbow Touch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Elbow Touch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Elbow Touch', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9e9f1a21-c6cc-4143-bfd4-744841ef25f7', 'Hamstring Curl Kick (Gymnastic Rings) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this curling exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '64791201', '64791201-Alternating-Hamstring-Curl-Kick-(female)_Plyometri.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. Ideal for hamstrings strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Hamstring Curl Kick - Alternating', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('9ea8527f-7548-4eaa-a79c-fa5ea2ec66c0', 'Standing Hip Frontal Rotation Curl', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this curling exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '57691201', '57691201-Standing-Hip-Frontal-Rotation-Curl-(female)_Plyome.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Standing Hip Frontal Rotation Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9eb2569f-830d-4273-bb26-443e189ada0c', 'Decline Bench Press (Smith Machine)', 'Chest', 'Smith Machine, Decline Bench', '{Pectorals}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '7531201', '07531201-Smith-Decline-Bench-Press_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Decline Bench Press. 2. Set the bench to a decline angle and secure your feet. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Decline Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 96, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'decline_press', 'Smith Decline Bench Press', 'Decline Bench Press', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('9eb467b2-1b03-4e3a-855c-6724b4ec799f', 'Bent Arm Pullover (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pulling movement targeting your chest. The lats, triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '13161201', '13161201-Barbell-Bent-Arm-Pullover_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Bent Arm Pullover. 2. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 3. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Bent Arm Pullover', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('9eb79cc9-45d6-413b-b1c9-b55296db2881', 'Flutter Kicks', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Flutter Kicks is a lower body kicking exercise that targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '46431201', '46431201-Flutter-Kicks-(version-3)-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Flutter Kicks. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Flutter Kicks', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('9ed697c4-b9e5-4c92-8e90-625be85edfbf', 'Lying Prone Y Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'The Lying Prone Y Raise is a raising exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '87191201', '87191201-Lyine-Prone-Y-Raise-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Lie face down with your body in a straight line. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Lying Prone Y Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lying Prone Y Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65);
